 "Build a high-quality profile (2-pass)": "制作高质量配置文件（两轮）",
 "Build a profile from an existing measurement": "从已有测量生成配置文件",
 "Build from the currently loaded patch set (attach its .ti1)": "从当前加载的色块集生成（附上它的 .ti1）",
 "Build my first ICC profile": "制作我的第一个ICC配置文件",
 "Building Profile…": "正在生成配置文件…",
 "Builds a more accurate profile by REUSING the measurements you already made for an earlier profile, instead of throwing them away.\n\nNormally, every profiling run starts from scratch: you print a chart, measure it, and build a profile from only those patches. If you later make a second, refined chart for the same printer and paper, the measurements from the first run are not used again.\n\nWith this option ON, ChromIQ can carry those earlier measurements forward. Here is the whole journey, step by step:\n\n  1. In Create Chart, you tick \"Refinement profile\" and pick the ICC profile from your earlier run. ChromIQ quietly keeps a copy of that profile's measurement data (a \"pre_…\" file) inside the working folder, so it is not deleted when the new chart is generated.\n\n  2. You print and measure the new chart as usual. In the Measure tab a new option appears: \"Also use measurement data from the pre-conditioning profile\". It only shows up when such saved data is actually present.\n\n  3. When you build the profile, ChromIQ combines the new measurements with the saved earlier ones and builds from the larger, combined set. More measured colours generally means a more accurate profile.\n\nYour freshly measured file is never altered — the combining happens on a separate copy only at build time, so you can re-measure or refine individual strips in Check & Refine exactly as before. The guided Check & Refine analysis still looks only at the strips you physically printed, so it will never ask you to re-measure a patch that came from the earlier run.\n\nWhen this option is OFF, ChromIQ behaves exactly as it always has — nothing in your normal workflow changes. Leave it off unless you specifically want to reuse measurements across refinement runs.": "通过重复利用你先前为旧配置文件所做的测量来生成更精确的配置文件，而不是把它们丢掉。\n\n通常每次配置文件制作都从零开始: 打印色卡、测量、只用这些色块生成配置文件。如果之后为同一台打印机和同种纸再做第二张优化色卡，第一轮的测量不会被再次使用。\n\n开启此选项后，ChromIQ可以把那些早先的测量带到后面。完整流程如下:\n\n  1. 在创建色卡中勾选「优化配置文件」并选择先前那一轮的ICC配置文件。ChromIQ会悄悄在工作文件夹里保留该配置文件测量数据的副本（一个「pre_…」文件），生成新色卡时不会删除它。\n\n  2. 照常打印并测量新色卡。测量标签页会出现一个新选项:「同时使用预调节配置文件的测量数据」。只有当确实存在这样的已保存数据时才会显示。\n\n  3. 生成配置文件时，ChromIQ把新测量与保存的旧测量合并，并基于更大的合并集合生成。测得的颜色越多，配置文件通常越精确。\n\n你新测量的文件绝不会被改动 — 合并只在生成时于单独的副本上进行，所以你仍可以像以前一样在检查与优化中重新测量或优化个别色条。引导式的检查与优化分析也只看你实际打印的色条，绝不会要求你重新测量来自旧一轮的色块。\n\n此选项关闭时，ChromIQ的行为与以往完全相同 — 你的正常工作流程不会有任何变化。除非你确实想在优化轮次间复用测量，否则保持关闭。",
 "Built on ArgyllCMS by Graeme Gill · Made possible by Knut Georg Larsson · Testing & feedback: Nelson (Pharmacist), Alan Goldhammer": "基于Graeme Gill的ArgyllCMS构建 · 感谢Knut Georg Larsson让一切成为可能 · 测试与反馈: Nelson (Pharmacist)、Alan Goldhammer",
 "Built-in preset — patch recipe changed ({notes}):\nBuilds a fresh chart from your settings — the patches will NOT match the preset.": "内置预设 — 色块配方已更改（{notes}）:\n按你的设置生成全新色卡 — 色块将不再与预设一致。",
 "Built-in preset — re-laid out ({notes}):\nRe-arranges the preset's exact patches on the page (targen skipped).": "内置预设 — 重新排版（{notes}）:\n把预设的原有色块在页面上重新排布（跳过targen）。",
 "Built-in preset — ready-made chart:\nCopies the bundled patch set as-is (targen and printtarg skipped).\nUnlock \"Edit page layout\" to re-arrange the same patches, or \"Edit patch recipe\" to build a different chart.": "内置预设 — 现成色卡:\n原样复制随附的色块集（跳过targen和printtarg）。\n解锁「编辑页面布局」可重新排布同样的色块，解锁「编辑色块配方」可生成不同的色卡。",
 "Built-in presets": "内置预设",
